A||||26||GT Bastard||Took the Fiero to the track... Funny stuff||||2||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||06-03-2000||10:58 PM||||A friend of mine here in town is hosting a thirdgen f-body gathering, and he invited me to the track with them.  I VERY QUICKLY fixed my coolant leak and called the local Fiero fanatic here in Sioux Falls.  His name is Brad, and he currently has something like 7 or 8 Fiero's.  Anyhow, I called him and said: "How do you feel about the race track?"  He replied: "I feel good about it, but if I'm not there in 20 minutes, I won't be able to come."  Anyhow, he didn't show up so we left without him.  Just so you know, Brad has a very queer '86 SE that he swapped a 3.1 motor into.  And his car hauls ass like you wouldn't believe(for a V6.)  Anyhow, me and the f-body guys make it to the track and I passed inspection!!! So I pay my 25 bucks and 4 hours later, the races start. Luckily, Brad eventually shows up with his SE! First up were the cars running slicks.  Only problem was, after 4 of them ran we were rained-out!!!  We sat around for 2 hours while the track dried, and it began to rain again..... Crap. The good news is, we saw some cool cars, met some cool people, and I got those nifty markings put on my quarter panel!  It just says "X209 T/T"<P>Misc. rambling begins...<P>So anyhow, I'm going to drive around tomorrow with those nifty marking on my car so people think I'm a bada$$.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyhow, as Brad and I start heading home, we each did a massive burnout on the slightly damp pavement.  We both kicked it sideways and left some nice scorch marks.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So we're screaming down these back country roads with Brad in the lead, and all of a sudden I see him smoke this beaver(or some other large rodent) that was walking down the highway.  I generally don't think the senseless murder of animals is funny, but there was something humerous about the way it flew end-over-end and barely missed me. surprisingly, his car didn't seem damaged. Not sure how that happened....  <P>Also.... When we hit the interstate off-ramp we spotted a HEAVILY riced Honda Accord, and we both promptly nailed it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The guy didn't even try to race us unfortunately.  It was fun to play with him on the interstate anyhow.  Brad and I also had some really sweet high speed runs with each other when traffic was sparse.  Very VERY fun.  <P>later boys...<P>||||reg||2
Z||000001||stimpy||06-04-2000||12:20 AM||||Once a few years ago I was driving down I-5 from Stockton to Tracy in a nasty windy storm. For those of you unfamilar, this is a long straight freeway going through rural area in Central California. I was going +-80mph in the southbound lanes when I saw something tumbling across the northbound lanes. I was in the fast lane naturally, and as the object came across the grass median, I saw that it was the most terrified looking chicken in the world. Poor thing was scrabbling at the pavement with his little chicken feet, wide-eyed and open beaked. I did my best to slow down, but with a car to my right and in nasty weather, it was either him or me. The little plume of feathers that came out from under the rear bumper gave a new meaning to the term "rooster tail"! I felt evil, but I laughed my ass off the rest of the way home. Sick, huh?||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||06-04-2000||02:36 AM||||HAHAHAhAHA, im still laughing about how he hit the large rodent and it flew end-over end, HAHAHAHAHAHA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Trien to kill me??? hahaha||||reg||10
Z||000003||Uaana||06-04-2000||02:36 AM||||Thats It!!!<BR>I'm calling PETA!!!<BR>Chrissy and the rest of the gang will come and get you fossil fuel burning neanderthals. Don't you know you should have killed yourself rather than hurt a fellow, peace loveing, natural to the environment, innocent animal!!!<BR>you things make me sick!!!!<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000004||Uaana||06-04-2000||02:38 AM||||Please ignore the previous post..<BR>Been spending too much time with the hippies at work..<P>Nuke a godless baby seal for christ!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||06-04-2000||02:41 AM||||GT Bastard - This is pretty weird, but are you talking about Brad Mundahl?  I know there cant be 2 brads in Sioux Falls with a ton of Fieros.....  Anyhow, my aunt knows his sister or something like that, so she gave me his phone number.  She said there is some sort of Fiero group in Sioux Falls where a bunch of people get to gether with Brad?  I'm gettin my Fiero painted in mid-July, but I really want it changed into a fastback befor I do.  Does he have the parts or know where I can get the parts to switch it over?  I have an 86 SE V-6, the rear bumper is the same (i think) as the fastbacks.<P>I have been meaning to call the guy, forever.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||06-04-2000||02:52 AM||||That's the same guy... He's a real nice fellow.  And yes, he can easily do that fastback swap.  He has the parts, but I'm not sure if they're up for grabs or not.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||frontal lobe||06-04-2000||02:53 AM||||First let me say that I, too, would never intentionally hurt a defenseless animal.  However, if an animal accidently takes one in a somewhat comical situation, I have no guilt about LOL, which I have been doing, although there are no witnesses.<P>Here's mine.  I'm on a long drive home one night about 11:30PM.  My wife is sound asleep.  I'm cruising down a 2-lane very rural highway at about 85mph when suddenly a farm cat walks right onto the highway in front of me.  If I SLAM on the brakes it's possible I miss the cat, but for sure I will maximum give my wife a heart attack and minimum make her wet herself.  I have about 1/2 second to decide so I just keep on the gas.  There is the typical whump-whump enough to make my wife half wake up and mumble, "What was that?"  Oh nothing, dear, go back to sleep.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||06-04-2000||11:17 AM||||Many years ago, late at night, I was driving home from the lake. Suddenly a 'possum waddled into view, smack in the middle of my lane.<BR>Going around was completely out of the question. So I decided to "split the difference", and straddle him. <BR>Unfortunately, I was driving my friend's Monza. Had the ground clearance of a skateboard. Ended up knocking him on the head, judging from the sound. Thonk! <BR>Everyone in the car went <I>"Eeeeeewwww!!!"</I> <BR>BTW... I normally do everything I can to miss "waddling livestock", but sometimes they are just determined... ||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||06-04-2000||11:41 AM||||Down around these parts (Texas/Oklahoma) we have been going through armadillo mating season. Those things get startled as you drive over them and jump up into your undercarriage. Pickup trucks don't even clear them! ||||reg||1
Z||000010||lowCG||06-04-2000||01:22 PM||||The only time I've had a near collision with one of our four-legged friends was when a small red fox passed under my car and exited off to the side in a flash while I was locking the binders.<BR>Have a buddy who wasn't so lucky however,when his recently completed '76Capri(3.0,balanced,Bilsteins,body mods,new paint,interior) nearly missed a fairly large Bovine(think it was a Holstein)on a corner.There was a rock face waiting to slow him down once he'd rotated around the lethargic animal and that was the end of that car.The paint wasn't even fully cured yet.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||06-04-2000||02:13 PM||||Back in the early 80's A buch of us were driving from Chicago up to Wisconsin Dells in a 77 Z28 Camero. It was in the evening and a Raccoon ran across the road with no time to stop. There was a large thump and a loud crack! We stopped and looked at the front end. The entire lower skirt of the air dam was missing! We drove back up the road but never found the Raccoon nor the air dam!||||reg||1
Z||000012||2birds||06-04-2000||03:35 PM||||<BR>I thought armadillos were born squashed, until I had a live one walk right into the shop the other day while I was changing tranny fluid on my T-bird.  They must be attracted to cars.  Walked right up to me while the car was on the lift.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||deceler8||06-04-2000||06:32 PM||||Was driving down I-29 the other day and there was a prairie dog just sitting in the right hand lane...traffic was very light. I kept going, thinking he was going to move eventually...he never did. I went right over the top of him, and looked in the rearview mirror and he was still sitting there except I saw his head move to look at me and then he moseyed over into the ditch.<P>Never knew prairie dogs could limbo.||||reg||1
Z||000014||olympic||06-04-2000||07:12 PM||||  Here's a couple of my experiences.<BR>-  I had a duck fly into the side of my    motorcycle at 60 mph, I almost lost    control.<BR>-  had a water beetle hit my face shield.  It    sounded like a rock had hit my helmet and    the splatter completely obscured my    vision.<BR>-  ran over a rabbit at 85 mph an a gravel      road.  All I saw in the mirror was white     fluff come out the back of my car.<BR>-  a deer jumped right over the hood of my      car while I was going about 40 mph.          Some gravel actually dropped from its    hooves onto the hood.<BR>-  several close calls with drunks/dumbasses    walking down the road at night.<BR>-  I drove through a herd of deer standing      all over the highway while I was going 120    mph.  This one was by far the scariest       ever.  <BR>  When I look back, I wonder how I ever lived through my teenage years with all the dumb stuff I did.||||reg||1
Z||000015||BN Boomer||06-04-2000||11:12 PM||||I once nailed about a dozen deer in the course of around 10 miles. Everytime I came around a corner there were more in my way and they would try to outrun me rather than just getting out of the way. Ugh, what a mess that was. The sound of bones snapping was disgusting.||||reg||4
Z||000016||stimpy||06-04-2000||11:17 PM||||Does LeBra make a model for a locamotive? I can imagine that cleaning that mess off was an interesting chore. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Pontiaddict||06-04-2000||11:34 PM||||I was riding with my dad on his motorcycle when a bird, a dove I think  comes from out of nowhere and hits him right in the helmet. I didn't notice until I  see his head fly back and this ball of feathers bounce off his head. It made a loud THWACK sound. (Louder for my dad) he almost loses control of the bike as we're heading toward this hill/curve. When we didn't die we were laughin our heads off. The bird must have survived the incident because it never hit the ground.||||reg||1
Z||000018||wilburt||06-05-2000||07:58 AM||||Bought a brand new '79 Trans Am. The second day I had it, three friends and I were out and I ran over a large grocery bag. Turned out to be a dead dog. Felt it roll under the floorboard.  I didn't know it hooked itself to the mufflers till we smelled the most awful stench. Had a hard time pushing him out with a stick, all gooey and all.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Shadow Wolf||06-07-2000||01:57 AM||||Was driving an 88 Turbo Sprint for a few years, and was one day taking the backroad into town.  So I get up to a nice comfortable crusing speed (about 90mph) and a robin drive-bombed the car.  Needless to say, I felt the usual 'thunk' on the front end.  Now, I felt bad for the bird, until I checked the front end about an hour later (for damage, of course) and the damn bird was still stuck to the centre post on the grille!  ||||reg||4
Z||000020||William||06-07-2000||10:53 PM||||Well, guess I will tell mine now. Several years ago I was driving to a new friends house at night. I was in my 79 camaro and was headed down the long dirt road he lived on at about 45 mph. An armadillo ran across the road and I hit him hearing that clump clump sound as my tires rolled over him. I really didn't think much about it and continued on. A couple hours later I was headed back home when I noticed something in the road,(I had forgotten about the armadillo), I suddenly saw two glowing eyes peer at me as the animal tried to get up and move out of the way. Clump clump, I got him a second time. It was as if he reconized the car and used his last bit life to avoid me. I have always assummed I will burn in hell for that incident.||||reg||4
Z||000021||Sage||06-07-2000||11:34 PM||||Have hit a couple cats, possums,and a ground hog, all unavoidable.  Never anything larger than that.  Had a deer kick the front fender of my Toyota truck as I swerved to miss it.<P>The funniest thing I have ever had happen with a critter was when we lived in Miami, Fla. and owned a Triumph TR-250 (which  is an English sports car with an inline 6 and a four spd.)I was headed up I-95 between Miami and Ft.Lauderdale doing about 70.  This car, for those that aren't familiar with them, has a cowl vent in front of the windshield that opens from inside the car.  I had it up to let fresh air into the floor(it was a rag top, but you got heat from the engine on your legs). All of a sudden, a field mouse pops his head up from the vent!  He jumps up out of the hole, runs to one side of the car looks over the side...runs to the other side of the car, looks over the side...then goes back to the other side and does a swan dive out into the air!(and traffic!)  I laugh everytime I remember it, even now.  I guess you had to be there.<P>Figure it must have been Mighty Mouse!?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||pollock||06-08-2000||10:02 AM||||My buddy's dad is a railroad engineer.  He once rounded a bend right into a whole herd of cattle standing on the track.  <P>Try that in your fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000023||blayde8||06-08-2000||12:50 PM||||Now this wasn't in a car, but still pretty funny.  <BR>One day I was mountain biking on a heavily wooded trail about 2 miles from my house.  I was going really fast so I was paying most of my attention to my sterring.  Then I took a glance up and saw a big blurry brown thing about 15 feet in front of me.  I got it in focus and noticed it was a pack of deer, big deer, about 6 of them.  I slammed on my brakes...a little too hard and my biked flipped over-and so did I.  I knew what was happening and while I was in the air I was thinking, "Sh*t, I'm going to land right on one of the deer."  Luckily, the deer started to run and only my right leg hit one of them. I stayed on the ground for about 2 min. with my eyes closed and not moving, I didn't know where they went.  I opened my eyes and saw all 6 of the deer staring at me.  They were about 15 feet away from me. I bet they were all laughing at me. So there I was, on the ground, not moving.  There were 2 males.  I had to wait 20 min. before they moved.  I didn't get hurt except for my back hurt.  My bike was fine too!<BR>  I still see those deer when I go back there, and whenever I pass them, they stare at me and I bet they laugh.||||reg||7
Z||000024||bHooper||06-08-2000||03:03 PM||||I have had several runin's with various critters.  While I can't remember all of the tree rats (squirl's for you city people) or turtle's I have encountered, I can remember the larger one's well.<P>The first was a encounter with a white horse.  It was 2 AM, I was driving back from my girlfiends house... down a country road.  When I rounded a corner, ~70 MPH, there was a white horse in the middle of the damn road!  I layed on the brakes (and horn), the car spun sideways and I stopped about 3 feet from him!... Sacred shitless, but not as bad as the second story.<P>The second, and scariest one happened about 11:30 at night on another country road.  I was in my CRX, doing ~85 MPH, topped a hill, and there stood an <B>entire herd of cattle</B>.  There was nothing I could, so I turned my head over my left sholder and closed my eyes, while wobling the steering wheel side to side.  At the point that I figured I shoulda hit something, I opened my eyes and saw a <B>giant white cow face</B> stareing at me!<P>Surprisingly, I hit nothing and imerged unscathed!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000025||Fret Naught||06-08-2000||05:51 PM||||OK My turn to Lie, though I doubt I can beat that last one. I wierdest thing I ever hit, it got stuck in my windshield wiper, got home and checked it out, it was a Bat!!! the kids got a real kick out of seeing one up close. They are quick, this one must of eaten some rotten berries cause he just flew right into the window||||reg||1
Z||000026||BN Boomer||06-08-2000||06:04 PM||||He he, Fret, I actually that happen to me a few months agn in my Suburban. At first I thought a mouse had fallen out of tree or something and landed on my windshield. When I stooped and pick it out of the windshield wiper and saw that it had wings, the wife kids got all freaked out. I thought it was pretty funny, though!||||reg||1
